1
00:00:03,837 --> 00:00:05,005
Then what about Pavi?

2
00:00:05,130 --> 00:00:07,298
Why didn't our parents
tell you about her?

3
00:00:07,299 --> 00:00:10,761
Did our parents think
I couldn't be the Avatar

4
00:00:11,178 --> 00:00:12,637
'cause of my leg?

5
00:00:12,638 --> 00:00:15,265
<i>Kayoko,
we need reinforcements.</i>

6
00:00:15,390 --> 00:00:17,183
<i>Let's reach out
to the other havens</i>

7
00:00:17,184 --> 00:00:18,185
<i>for more benders.</i>

8
00:00:18,602 --> 00:00:20,729
<i>We know how
to take care of ourselves.</i>

9
00:00:23,273 --> 00:00:24,942
<i>It is coming.</i>

10
00:00:25,442 --> 00:00:26,527
What's coming?

11
00:00:26,652 --> 00:00:29,112
Commander!

12
00:00:40,958 --> 00:00:42,375
Thanks for your help, Tala.

13
00:00:42,376 --> 00:00:44,168
I know you need
to get back to your squad.

14
00:00:44,169 --> 00:00:46,671
No rest for the weary.

15
00:00:46,672 --> 00:00:48,715
I'm burning the candle
from both ends,

16
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:50,258
but you're welcome.

17
00:00:50,259 --> 00:00:52,134
Thanks to Kayoko,

18
00:00:52,135 --> 00:00:53,594
we're working around the clock!

19
00:00:53,595 --> 00:00:56,098
- We'll get a day off soon.
- I hope so.

20
00:00:56,557 --> 00:00:58,307
I'm exhausted.

21
00:00:58,308 --> 00:01:00,017
We shouldn't even be out here!

22
00:01:00,018 --> 00:01:02,604
I heard the Faceless nabbed
another bender last night

23
00:01:02,729 --> 00:01:04,104
and two the night before.

24
00:01:04,105 --> 00:01:06,357
Our friend Uki went missing
a few weeks ago.

25
00:01:06,358 --> 00:01:08,693
See! It's open season on benders

26
00:01:08,694 --> 00:01:11,446
and we're out here like a bunch
of sitting duck-rabbits!

27
00:01:12,573 --> 00:01:14,198
Huh!

28
00:01:17,035 --> 00:01:19,121
Ah!

29
00:01:19,997 --> 00:01:21,164
Tala!

30
00:01:21,290 --> 00:01:22,874
Bender down!

31
00:01:24,543 --> 00:01:25,918
I'm so sorry, Tala!

32
00:01:25,919 --> 00:01:27,796
I can't look.

33
00:01:28,130 --> 00:01:29,130
How bad is it?

34
00:01:34,052 --> 00:01:35,761
Daemin, take Tala
to the hospital.

35
00:01:35,762 --> 00:01:37,598
Lan and I
will finish sealing this up.

36
00:01:37,723 --> 00:01:39,348
You know, It looks... painful,

37
00:01:39,349 --> 00:01:41,559
but aesthetically pleasing.

38
00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:43,895
This is all my fault.

39
00:01:44,021 --> 00:01:45,897
I'm just so tired.

40
00:01:46,023 --> 00:01:47,857
I can barely see straight.

41
00:01:47,858 --> 00:01:49,317
It was an accident.

42
00:01:49,318 --> 00:01:51,528
Come on, let's make sure
no one else gets hurt

43
00:01:51,653 --> 00:01:52,570
by this thing.

44
00:01:52,571 --> 00:01:54,947
How? It won't stop growing!

45
00:01:54,948 --> 00:01:56,950
If the Chancellor
would just listen to us

46
00:01:57,075 --> 00:01:58,869
instead of making
ridiculous demands, then we--

47
00:01:58,994 --> 00:02:00,037
Enough, Varun.

48
00:02:00,162 --> 00:02:01,663
We've got a job to do.

49
00:02:09,880 --> 00:02:11,173
<i>Fire.</i>

50
00:02:11,673 --> 00:02:12,923
<i>Air.</i>

51
00:02:12,924 --> 00:02:14,051
<i>Water.</i>

52
00:02:14,593 --> 00:02:15,385
<i>Earth.</i>

53
00:02:17,054 --> 00:02:18,971
<i>Long ago, the Avatar,</i>

54
00:02:18,972 --> 00:02:21,183
<i>master of all four elements,</i>

55
00:02:21,308 --> 00:02:23,851
<i>brought forth the Cataclysm.</i>

56
00:02:23,852 --> 00:02:25,311
<i>Out of the devastation,</i>

57
00:02:25,312 --> 00:02:28,147
<i>the world built
the Seven Havens.</i>

58
00:02:28,148 --> 00:02:29,983
<i>Now the Avatar has returned,</i>

59
00:02:30,108 --> 00:02:33,236
<i>but for the first time,
there are two.</i>

60
00:02:33,654 --> 00:02:35,697
<i>Most fear they'll destroy
the world again.</i>

61
00:02:36,156 --> 00:02:39,242
<i>But I believe
they will save it.</i>

62
00:02:59,388 --> 00:03:01,306
Ow, ow, ow.

63
00:03:01,431 --> 00:03:02,641
Need help, sis?

64
00:03:02,974 --> 00:03:03,975
No!

65
00:03:04,393 --> 00:03:05,310
Ow!

66
00:03:12,275 --> 00:03:13,359
Are you okay?

67
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:14,403
I'm fine!

68
00:03:15,070 --> 00:03:18,824
I'm working on my, uh,
Spinning Top stance.

69
00:03:19,199 --> 00:03:20,825
You probably
haven't heard of it.

70
00:03:20,826 --> 00:03:22,077
Right.

71
00:03:22,411 --> 00:03:24,079
Look, it's okay
if you're struggling.

72
00:03:24,204 --> 00:03:26,123
I've had years of training.

73
00:03:26,248 --> 00:03:27,624
You'll catch up someday.

74
00:03:27,999 --> 00:03:29,584
What if I don't?

75
00:03:30,252 --> 00:03:32,129
Maybe our parents were right.

76
00:03:32,546 --> 00:03:34,131
Maybe I am a dud.

77
00:03:34,256 --> 00:03:35,339
Don't worry!

78
00:03:35,340 --> 00:03:36,925
You can be...

79
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:38,885
the Avatar's sidekick?

80
00:03:39,344 --> 00:03:41,804
My little buddy... dirt girl!

81
00:03:41,805 --> 00:03:43,223
Pavi, what's this about?

82
00:03:43,348 --> 00:03:45,683
She can't train
'cause her bad leg hurts.

83
00:03:45,684 --> 00:03:46,518
Again.

84
00:03:46,643 --> 00:03:48,102
It's not "bad."

85
00:03:48,103 --> 00:03:49,229
It's just different.

86
00:03:49,354 --> 00:03:52,148
And it hurts less
when I sit like this.

87
00:03:52,149 --> 00:03:53,275
She's woken up crying

88
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:55,652
every night this week
because of her leg.

89
00:03:55,777 --> 00:03:56,737
I'm fine!

90
00:03:57,404 --> 00:03:58,488
Be that as it may,

91
00:03:58,613 --> 00:04:00,614
perhaps you should see a doctor.

92
00:04:00,615 --> 00:04:02,284
A doctor?

93
00:04:02,409 --> 00:04:04,244
No, no, no, I don't want
my brain scrambled

94
00:04:04,369 --> 00:04:05,411
or my blood sucked out!

95
00:04:05,412 --> 00:04:07,705
That is not at all what hap--

96
00:04:07,706 --> 00:04:10,332
Wait, hang on. Have you never
been seen by a doctor?

97
00:04:10,333 --> 00:04:12,210
Nope! And look at me!

98
00:04:12,335 --> 00:04:14,171
I am in perfect-- Ow!

99
00:04:14,296 --> 00:04:16,882
Ow, ow, ow, ow ow, ow, ow, ow!

100
00:04:17,966 --> 00:04:19,008
Can I go with Pavi?

101
00:04:19,009 --> 00:04:20,427
She needs my courage.

102
00:04:20,552 --> 00:04:22,179
No, I don't!

103
00:04:22,304 --> 00:04:24,055
I'm not a scaredy cat-monkey!

104
00:04:25,515 --> 00:04:27,433
No, no, no, no, no. No.

105
00:04:27,434 --> 00:04:29,811
You are my brave little baby...

106
00:04:30,937 --> 00:04:33,565
...who's scared of everything.

107
00:04:37,527 --> 00:04:39,069
Prove you're not scared.

108
00:04:39,070 --> 00:04:40,113
Fine!

109
00:04:40,530 --> 00:04:41,947
I'll go see the doctor

110
00:04:41,948 --> 00:04:43,909
even though I don't need to.

111
00:04:52,542 --> 00:04:54,211
I made the thingamajig
for my leg

112
00:04:54,336 --> 00:04:57,005
'cause I got tired
of hopping around all the time.

113
00:04:57,130 --> 00:04:58,547
Very resourceful.

114
00:04:58,548 --> 00:05:00,841
You need to be nice
to your sound leg.

115
00:05:00,842 --> 00:05:03,761
No hopping unless
it's absolutely necessary.

116
00:05:03,762 --> 00:05:05,055
"Sound"?

117
00:05:05,430 --> 00:05:06,765
Legs can't hear.

118
00:05:07,140 --> 00:05:09,600
See, I told you
doctors were weird.

119
00:05:09,601 --> 00:05:11,769
Her other leg always hurts.

120
00:05:11,770 --> 00:05:13,063
It's really sad.

121
00:05:13,188 --> 00:05:15,064
No! N-No, it's not!

122
00:05:15,065 --> 00:05:17,107
Stop feeling sad for me.

123
00:05:17,108 --> 00:05:18,108
Sorry.

124
00:05:18,109 --> 00:05:19,944
If you like,
you can use a crutch

125
00:05:19,945 --> 00:05:22,280
while I fashion
a new prosthetic for you.

126
00:05:22,864 --> 00:05:24,366
That should make things better.

127
00:05:24,491 --> 00:05:27,077
Unfortunately,
some of what you're experiencing

128
00:05:27,202 --> 00:05:28,662
is phantom limb pain.

129
00:05:28,787 --> 00:05:31,498
It's very common
after the loss of a limb.

130
00:05:33,166 --> 00:05:35,584
But I didn't lose my leg.

131
00:05:35,585 --> 00:05:37,212
I was born like this.

132
00:05:37,629 --> 00:05:39,338
Hmm. I'm fairly certain

133
00:05:39,339 --> 00:05:40,715
you lost the lower part
of your leg

134
00:05:40,841 --> 00:05:42,384
within the past few years.

135
00:05:42,509 --> 00:05:44,593
How'd you forget
you lost your leg?

136
00:05:45,637 --> 00:05:47,347
The mind sometimes
protects itself

137
00:05:47,472 --> 00:05:48,807
from painful memories.

138
00:05:50,475 --> 00:05:52,269
Have we found
an effective treatment

139
00:05:52,394 --> 00:05:53,228
for the Affliction?

140
00:05:53,353 --> 00:05:54,812
Not yet.

141
00:05:54,813 --> 00:05:55,980
The first wave of Afflicted

142
00:05:55,981 --> 00:05:57,565
were struck by The Anomaly.

143
00:05:57,566 --> 00:06:01,068
But now, Ellorans are becoming
spontaneously Afflicted,

144
00:06:01,069 --> 00:06:02,695
coming in
with the same symptoms.

145
00:06:02,696 --> 00:06:05,991
Fear, hallucinations,
those red eyes.

146
00:06:06,658 --> 00:06:07,950
It's baffling!

147
00:06:07,951 --> 00:06:09,368
They're out to get me!

148
00:06:09,369 --> 00:06:10,619
I can't sleep!

149
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:11,830
They're out to get me.

150
00:06:11,955 --> 00:06:13,498
They're everywhere...

151
00:06:16,293 --> 00:06:17,460
Tala!

152
00:06:17,836 --> 00:06:19,003
What happened?

153
00:06:19,004 --> 00:06:20,921
Sir! Are the Faceless back?

154
00:06:20,922 --> 00:06:22,172
Did the alarm sound?

155
00:06:22,173 --> 00:06:24,509
- I can fight! I-I can--
- All will be well.

156
00:06:24,926 --> 00:06:27,345
Get some rest. Okay?

157
00:06:30,015 --> 00:06:33,685
I'm sorry I haven't
come sooner, old friend.

158
00:06:34,352 --> 00:06:36,313
The doctor tells me
you're holding strong.

159
00:06:36,438 --> 00:06:37,480
The storm!

160
00:06:37,939 --> 00:06:39,232
Too strong!

161
00:06:39,357 --> 00:06:41,025
I can't stop it.

162
00:06:41,026 --> 00:06:42,819
Ellora's on the brink
of collapse.

163
00:06:42,944 --> 00:06:44,029
The Brigade, Kayoko,

164
00:06:44,154 --> 00:06:46,281
they're all turning to me
for answers.

165
00:06:47,198 --> 00:06:48,617
What should I do?

166
00:06:49,075 --> 00:06:51,703
I don't know. I don't...

167
00:06:53,038 --> 00:06:54,164
Karthik!

168
00:06:54,581 --> 00:06:55,790
I have a ghost leg!

169
00:06:56,207 --> 00:06:58,208
Or... ghost pain?

170
00:06:58,209 --> 00:07:01,712
That doc wasn't making
any sense.

171
00:07:01,713 --> 00:07:03,924
I told both of you
to wait in the main area

172
00:07:04,049 --> 00:07:04,883
of the hospital.

173
00:07:05,008 --> 00:07:06,342
It's not safe for you

174
00:07:06,343 --> 00:07:07,594
in the Afflicted Ward.

175
00:07:12,682 --> 00:07:13,807
That's her!

176
00:07:13,808 --> 00:07:15,852
She's the Avatar!

177
00:07:16,227 --> 00:07:17,519
Easy, friend.

178
00:07:17,520 --> 00:07:18,812
I was right!

179
00:07:18,813 --> 00:07:22,025
The Brigade's in league
with the Avatar!

180
00:07:22,442 --> 00:07:24,318
You are a traitor to Ellora!

181
00:07:24,319 --> 00:07:25,694
He's not a traitor.

182
00:07:25,695 --> 00:07:27,196
He's a great commander!

183
00:07:27,197 --> 00:07:28,156
That's enough!

184
00:07:28,281 --> 00:07:30,325
I'd be more careful
if I were you.

185
00:07:30,450 --> 00:07:31,867
If I really were the Avatar,

186
00:07:31,868 --> 00:07:33,661
that means
I'm the most powerful bender

187
00:07:33,662 --> 00:07:34,871
in the Seven Havens,

188
00:07:34,996 --> 00:07:36,163
so you'd better stop bullying

189
00:07:36,164 --> 00:07:37,748
Commander Karthik or else!

190
00:07:37,749 --> 00:07:41,252
The Avatar will destroy us!
Beware!

191
00:07:41,378 --> 00:07:44,088
Beware the Avatar.

192
00:07:44,089 --> 00:07:51,888
Beware the Avatar.

193
00:08:21,543 --> 00:08:22,668
The Avatar!

194
00:08:22,669 --> 00:08:24,379
The Avatar lives!

195
00:08:24,504 --> 00:08:26,922
Brigade, follow me!

196
00:08:29,384 --> 00:08:30,552
Are you hurt?

197
00:08:30,969 --> 00:08:32,804
I need to stop Bountan
and the others.

198
00:08:32,929 --> 00:08:35,431
They're a danger to themselves
and everyone in the hospital!

199
00:08:35,432 --> 00:08:36,724
Oh! Let me help.

200
00:08:36,725 --> 00:08:37,766
I can help too!

201
00:08:37,767 --> 00:08:39,184
How? You can barely stand.

202
00:08:40,395 --> 00:08:43,856
Both of you stay here.

203
00:08:43,857 --> 00:08:44,940
Out of harm's way.

204
00:08:44,941 --> 00:08:46,358
Just because I have one leg

205
00:08:46,359 --> 00:08:48,193
doesn't mean I can't do things!

206
00:08:48,194 --> 00:08:49,904
You know, when I was alone

207
00:08:50,030 --> 00:08:53,616
I did everything by myself
without anyone's help.

208
00:08:57,620 --> 00:08:59,789
Dr. Jia said no hopping!

209
00:09:03,001 --> 00:09:04,793
Can someone massage my neck?

210
00:09:04,794 --> 00:09:06,296
I can barely feel my feet.

211
00:09:06,421 --> 00:09:07,589
Poor Tala...

212
00:09:07,714 --> 00:09:09,882
Lan, stop beating yourself up.

213
00:09:09,883 --> 00:09:11,551
Yeah,
don't blame yourself.

214
00:09:11,676 --> 00:09:13,719
We've barely slept in weeks!

215
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:16,138
And the Faceless
are kidnapping benders

216
00:09:16,139 --> 00:09:17,640
whenever they feel like it!

217
00:09:17,766 --> 00:09:19,391
- Yeah, guess he's right.
- Mm-hmm.

218
00:09:19,392 --> 00:09:21,895
Being in the Brigade
was always such an honor.

219
00:09:22,312 --> 00:09:24,481
But now I wish
I wasn't a bender at all.

220
00:09:24,856 --> 00:09:26,648
I'd settle for being
a lousy cook.

221
00:09:26,649 --> 00:09:28,610
Uh... no offense.

222
00:09:28,735 --> 00:09:29,735
None taken.

223
00:09:29,736 --> 00:09:31,029
I'm far from lousy.

224
00:09:31,154 --> 00:09:33,448
But rather than grumbling
to each other,

225
00:09:33,573 --> 00:09:35,282
maybe you should take up
your grievances

226
00:09:35,283 --> 00:09:36,659
with Chancellor Kayoko.

227
00:09:36,785 --> 00:09:39,912
That would be
a huge breach of protocol.

228
00:09:39,913 --> 00:09:40,789
Says who?

229
00:09:40,914 --> 00:09:42,790
Let's go tell her what's what!

230
00:09:42,791 --> 00:09:43,832
Who's with me?

231
00:09:43,833 --> 00:09:45,335
Yeah. Let's go!

232
00:09:49,255 --> 00:09:51,882
Well, the Brigade
is an angry mob,

233
00:09:51,883 --> 00:09:53,634
but silver lining...

234
00:09:53,635 --> 00:09:54,760
free leftovers!

235
00:09:56,262 --> 00:09:57,305
Uh...

236
00:09:57,806 --> 00:09:58,973
Sorry, Jae.

237
00:09:59,099 --> 00:10:00,391
Lan, wait!

238
00:10:23,289 --> 00:10:25,375
The demon beast has found us!

239
00:10:36,761 --> 00:10:37,928
Put your arm over my shoulder.

240
00:10:37,929 --> 00:10:39,054
I'll be your crutch.

241
00:10:39,055 --> 00:10:40,305
I don't need help!

242
00:10:40,306 --> 00:10:42,391
Yes, you do!

243
00:10:42,392 --> 00:10:43,476
Why are you being a dunderhead?

244
00:10:43,601 --> 00:10:45,018
I don't know what that is,

245
00:10:45,019 --> 00:10:46,479
but I am not a dunderhead!

246
00:10:54,195 --> 00:10:57,614
Hurry! We must warn the council
about the Avatar!

247
00:11:01,953 --> 00:11:03,829
This isn't a training exercise.

248
00:11:03,830 --> 00:11:05,497
These Afflicted can hurt you.

249
00:11:05,498 --> 00:11:09,168
Just this once, I am giving you
permission to openly bend.

250
00:11:09,169 --> 00:11:11,379
I need you to work together.

251
00:11:11,504 --> 00:11:12,337
Understood?

252
00:11:12,338 --> 00:11:13,672
Mm.

253
00:11:13,673 --> 00:11:14,799
That noise earlier,

254
00:11:14,924 --> 00:11:16,925
it must have come
from the generator room.

255
00:11:16,926 --> 00:11:18,427
We must seal the doors
to the ward

256
00:11:18,428 --> 00:11:20,763
before the Afflicted escape
into the main hospital.

257
00:11:21,181 --> 00:11:22,265
Follow me.

258
00:11:42,744 --> 00:11:44,412
Pavi, wait here.

259
00:12:11,314 --> 00:12:12,941
Avatar!

260
00:12:20,490 --> 00:12:21,950
I'm sorry, Tala.

261
00:12:23,910 --> 00:12:26,329
Stupid ghost leg...

262
00:12:29,249 --> 00:12:30,875
No! Please, please, please,

263
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:32,793
d-do-don't hurt me.

264
00:12:34,504 --> 00:12:37,131
Red eyes. The camodillo.

265
00:12:37,757 --> 00:12:40,551
You're not mad, you're afraid.

266
00:12:40,885 --> 00:12:41,843
But why?

267
00:12:41,844 --> 00:12:43,805
Because you're the Avatar!

268
00:12:43,930 --> 00:12:45,807
Uh... nope!

269
00:12:45,932 --> 00:12:47,599
The Avatar has two legs.

270
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:48,935
I only got one. See?

271
00:12:50,478 --> 00:12:53,063
Is... Is that the Avatar?

272
00:12:53,064 --> 00:12:55,483
D-Don't worry! I'll... hide you!

273
00:13:02,573 --> 00:13:03,532
Don't make a peep.

274
00:13:03,533 --> 00:13:04,908
So cozy!

275
00:13:04,909 --> 00:13:06,160
Pavi, are you okay?

276
00:13:06,286 --> 00:13:08,037
- We heard you scream--
- Shh!

277
00:13:08,413 --> 00:13:10,622
The Molin guy
was scared of Nisha,

278
00:13:10,623 --> 00:13:11,957
so I wrapped him in the wall.

279
00:13:11,958 --> 00:13:12,959
Now he feels better.

280
00:13:13,543 --> 00:13:17,754
Perhaps fear isn't just
a symptom of the Affliction,

281
00:13:17,755 --> 00:13:19,006
but also the cause.

282
00:13:30,101 --> 00:13:31,728
The Avatar!

283
00:13:33,438 --> 00:13:34,605
Go back to the ward!

284
00:13:34,731 --> 00:13:36,065
They'll follow us there!

285
00:13:42,488 --> 00:13:44,323
Come on! Just let me help you!

286
00:13:44,324 --> 00:13:45,950
I told you before, I'm fi--

287
00:13:46,075 --> 00:13:48,285
- Ah!
- Pavi!

288
00:13:58,504 --> 00:13:59,504
Huh?

289
00:14:12,185 --> 00:14:13,269
Well done, girls.

290
00:14:13,394 --> 00:14:14,729
I think we stopped them.

291
00:14:16,481 --> 00:14:17,607
The demon beast...

292
00:14:17,732 --> 00:14:19,024
The Avatar?

293
00:14:19,025 --> 00:14:20,525
Ellora will not fall to you!

294
00:14:30,745 --> 00:14:31,829
It's your turn.

295
00:14:31,954 --> 00:14:32,955
Huh?

296
00:14:56,312 --> 00:14:58,022
We're afraid for our lives!

297
00:14:58,439 --> 00:15:00,775
What are you
gonna do to protect us?

298
00:15:01,859 --> 00:15:03,944
I know firsthand how hard it is

299
00:15:03,945 --> 00:15:05,738
to devote yourself
to your haven.

300
00:15:05,863 --> 00:15:09,617
My whole life has been focused
on the survival of Ellora.

301
00:15:10,159 --> 00:15:11,952
We are at a critical point,

302
00:15:11,953 --> 00:15:15,205
and I hate to ask
so much of our Brigade,

303
00:15:15,206 --> 00:15:17,707
but we must all make sacrifices

304
00:15:17,708 --> 00:15:19,042
to keep our haven safe.

305
00:15:19,043 --> 00:15:21,628
That's a load of camodillo dung!

306
00:15:21,629 --> 00:15:26,216
Keep benders safe!

307
00:15:26,217 --> 00:15:27,717
Keep benders safe!

308
00:15:27,718 --> 00:15:32,849
Keep benders safe!

309
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:35,976
Fellow benders!

310
00:15:35,977 --> 00:15:37,770
I know how hard it's been

311
00:15:37,895 --> 00:15:39,688
and how much we've sacrificed.

312
00:15:39,689 --> 00:15:42,108
But Chancellor Kayoko
is our ally.

313
00:15:42,525 --> 00:15:43,818
Let me talk to her.

314
00:15:47,697 --> 00:15:49,282
Karthik has taught you well.

315
00:15:49,657 --> 00:15:50,991
With respect, Chancellor,

316
00:15:50,992 --> 00:15:53,910
we benders are dedicated
to Ellora's safety.

317
00:15:53,911 --> 00:15:55,788
But I've already lost
two friends,

318
00:15:55,913 --> 00:15:56,789
Tala and Uki.

319
00:15:56,914 --> 00:15:58,708
I can't lose any more.

320
00:15:58,833 --> 00:16:00,960
Ellorans have always
survived adversity,

321
00:16:01,085 --> 00:16:02,919
no matter how difficult.

322
00:16:02,920 --> 00:16:04,254
But we've never encountered

323
00:16:04,255 --> 00:16:05,923
a threat like
The Anomaly before.

324
00:16:06,048 --> 00:16:07,633
Jae, if you're asking me
to reach out

325
00:16:07,758 --> 00:16:09,050
to the other havens,

326
00:16:09,051 --> 00:16:11,803
I've already told Karthik
that's impossible.

327
00:16:17,935 --> 00:16:20,353
Karthik trusts that you want
to protect Ellora,

328
00:16:20,354 --> 00:16:21,981
no matter the cost.

329
00:16:22,648 --> 00:16:25,526
What our home needs
right now is help.

330
00:16:25,943 --> 00:16:27,862
So what are you going to do?

331
00:16:42,126 --> 00:16:43,084
He's scared!

332
00:16:43,085 --> 00:16:45,171
You have to make him feel safe.

333
00:16:46,464 --> 00:16:48,382
Hello, old friend.

334
00:16:48,799 --> 00:16:50,301
Fancy a game of Dou-Shou-Gow?

335
00:16:54,180 --> 00:16:56,891
Yeah, you were always
more of a Pai Sho player!

336
00:17:10,655 --> 00:17:12,280
Have mercy on me!

337
00:17:12,281 --> 00:17:13,782
Bountan, remember
all that you and I

338
00:17:13,907 --> 00:17:14,991
have survived together.

339
00:17:14,992 --> 00:17:17,327
Firestorms in the Tong Desert,

340
00:17:17,328 --> 00:17:19,329
the-the siege at Crescent Bay,

341
00:17:19,454 --> 00:17:21,582
your mother's awful cooking.

342
00:17:22,375 --> 00:17:24,918
Karthik? Is that you?

343
00:17:24,919 --> 00:17:27,255
Yes, old friend. It's me.

344
00:17:27,838 --> 00:17:30,298
The spirit world
has unleashed its wrath.

345
00:17:30,299 --> 00:17:33,426
The fate of Ellora
is in your hands.

346
00:17:33,427 --> 00:17:34,887
What can I do?

347
00:17:35,555 --> 00:17:37,390
It's too late.

348
00:17:38,015 --> 00:17:39,141
Too late.

349
00:17:39,559 --> 00:17:41,143
Too late.

350
00:18:11,632 --> 00:18:13,883
The spirit world's wrath.

351
00:18:13,884 --> 00:18:16,220
The Anomaly knows you're scared!

352
00:18:31,902 --> 00:18:33,988
Karthik's in danger!

353
00:18:37,992 --> 00:18:38,993
Nisha!

354
00:18:39,869 --> 00:18:41,662
I need your help!

355
00:18:45,708 --> 00:18:46,834
Let's go!

356
00:18:48,419 --> 00:18:50,129
Girls, no!

357
00:19:22,161 --> 00:19:23,704
How many days?

358
00:19:24,121 --> 00:19:25,205
Two weeks.

359
00:19:25,206 --> 00:19:27,124
If we can survive
the Harshlands.

360
00:19:27,500 --> 00:19:29,251
We have no other choice.

361
00:19:29,710 --> 00:19:31,879
I don't know
if we're doing the right thing.

362
00:19:32,296 --> 00:19:34,882
Mom? Dad?

363
00:19:46,435 --> 00:19:48,604
Nisha! Pavi! Are you all right?

364
00:19:49,730 --> 00:19:51,773
How in the Seven Havens

365
00:19:51,774 --> 00:19:53,901
did you learn to energybend?

366
00:19:54,026 --> 00:19:56,362
Energy what?

367
00:20:06,956 --> 00:20:09,417
Sorry for being
a blunderhead.

368
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:11,377
Apology accepted.

369
00:20:11,711 --> 00:20:14,337
I just wanted
to prove that I can

370
00:20:14,338 --> 00:20:16,090
take care of myself.

371
00:20:16,841 --> 00:20:18,551
I know you can, but...

372
00:20:18,676 --> 00:20:20,678
when I see you hurting,
I want to help.

373
00:20:21,095 --> 00:20:25,015
When I need your help,
I promise to ask.

374
00:20:25,474 --> 00:20:27,309
But don't feel sad for me.

375
00:20:27,768 --> 00:20:31,313
It makes me feel sadder
for myself than I already do.

376
00:20:31,772 --> 00:20:33,107
What are you sad about?

377
00:20:34,400 --> 00:20:37,026
What if the White Lotus
decide I'm not good enough

378
00:20:37,027 --> 00:20:38,279
to train with you,

379
00:20:38,612 --> 00:20:39,822
and kick me out?

380
00:20:40,531 --> 00:20:42,742
I don't want to lose
my sister again.

381
00:20:43,951 --> 00:20:45,077
Are you kidding?

382
00:20:45,202 --> 00:20:47,163
I'd never let them kick you out!

383
00:20:47,538 --> 00:20:50,540
Besides, you and me kicked
The Anomaly's butt!

384
00:20:50,541 --> 00:20:51,917
And we did energybending.

385
00:20:52,042 --> 00:20:54,712
That's super advanced
Avatar stuff.

386
00:20:55,212 --> 00:20:57,298
I don't understand The Anomaly.

387
00:20:57,423 --> 00:20:59,133
It hurts other people,

388
00:20:59,258 --> 00:21:01,342
but it shows us

389
00:21:01,343 --> 00:21:03,052
memories of our mom and dad.

390
00:21:03,053 --> 00:21:05,097
I don't understand it either.

391
00:21:05,848 --> 00:21:08,476
Dr. Jia said
you lost your ghost leg

392
00:21:08,601 --> 00:21:10,311
in the past few years.

393
00:21:11,228 --> 00:21:13,022
I wonder if it happened when--

394
00:21:13,147 --> 00:21:14,690
When I lost you.

395
00:21:14,815 --> 00:21:16,150
And Mom and Dad!

396
00:21:16,484 --> 00:21:18,611
We have to find out
what happened to us.

397
00:21:33,542 --> 00:21:35,294
Ooh, bendy!

398
00:21:39,465 --> 00:21:41,842
Mmm.

399
00:21:46,764 --> 00:21:48,682
Calling any and all Havens.

400
00:21:48,808 --> 00:21:49,974
This is Ellora.

401
00:21:49,975 --> 00:21:52,269
I repeat, this is Ellora

402
00:21:52,394 --> 00:21:54,355
calling any and all Havens.

403
00:21:55,189 --> 00:21:56,440
<i>We need you.</i>

